---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { supabaseUrl } from "../lib/supabase-public";
const travelGuideHero = `${supabaseUrl}/storage/v1/object/public/materuni-images/waterfall_image/1791998303073-materuni-waterfall-hike.jpg`;
---
<SiteLayout title="Materuni Visitor Guide | Waterfall, Coffee & Village Tours" description="Plan a Materuni visit near Moshi with advice on waterfall walks, Chagga coffee, village culture, transport, trail conditions, weather and booking." preloadImage={travelGuideHero}>
<section class="media-hero" aria-labelledby="guide-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU VISIT</span><h1 id="guide-title">Prepare for a rewarding day in Materuni.</h1><p>A little preparation makes it easier to enjoy the forest paths, village hospitality and changing mountain weather. For detailed transport articles and cultural guides, visit our new <a href="/journal" style="color:#C5A059;text-decoration:underline">Materuni Journal →</a></p></div><img src={travelGuideHero} alt="Materuni Falls in the green foothills of Mount Kilimanjaro" width="1200" height="900" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></section>
<section class="section"><div class="split"><div><h2>Getting to Materuni</h2><p>Materuni Village is in the Kilimanjaro foothills near Moshi. Journey time and road conditions depend on your exact pickup point, traffic, weather and the village road. You can arrange your own transport or ask Materuni Hosts about a separate transfer quote. Share your pickup point, date and group size so the host can confirm availability, vehicle details, timing and price before you agree.</p><h2>What to wear and bring</h2><p>Wear comfortable clothes for walking and shoes with a reliable grip. The waterfall path can be wet, muddy or uneven, so sandals and smooth-soled shoes are not ideal. Bring a light rain layer, sun protection and a reusable water bottle. Keep your camera or phone protected from spray and rain.</p><h2>Walking and trail conditions</h2><p>Expect a nature walk rather than a paved promenade. Take your time on slippery sections, follow your guide’s instructions and let your host know in advance if anyone in your group has mobility concerns or would prefer a gentler pace.</p><h2>Food and dietary needs</h2><p>Local meals are part of several experiences. Please tell us about allergies, dietary preferences or accessibility needs when you send your booking request.</p></div><div><h2>Booking, payment & guarantees</h2><p>Submitting a booking request does not confirm or reserve a place, and no payment is taken by submitting the form. Your host must first confirm availability, the experience details, final price and any transfer arrangements in writing. Payment methods, timing, cancellation terms and any changes are agreed directly as part of the confirmed booking.</p>
<h2>Explore Materuni experiences</h2><p>Choose a locally hosted visit that suits your interests: <a href="/materuni-waterfall-tour">Materuni Waterfall and Chagga Village</a>, a <a href="/materuni-coffee-tour">traditional Chagga coffee experience</a>, or browse <a href="/experiences">all Materuni experiences</a>. For practical arrival advice, read <a href="/journal/how-to-get-to-materuni">how to get to Materuni from Moshi, Arusha and Kilimanjaro Airport</a>.</p><h2>Weather and waterfall conditions</h2><p>Mountain weather can change, and rain may affect the trail and waterfall conditions. Water levels, safe access and any opportunity to enter the water depend on conditions on the day. Your guide’s safety advice should always take priority.</p><h2>Respectful village visits</h2><p>Materuni is a living community, not a staged attraction. Be considerate around homes and farms, ask before photographing people and follow your host’s guidance when visiting community spaces. Take your litter with you and avoid disturbing plants or wildlife along the trail.</p><h2>Before you travel</h2><p>Confirm your pickup point, start time, group size and any dietary or accessibility needs with your host. If the weather changes or you are unsure what to bring, ask us before setting off.</p><a class="button" href="https://wa.me/255612068540" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a></div></div></section>
<style>.media-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(280px,.9fr);gap:clamp(24px,5vw,64px);align-items:center;padding:clamp(42px,7vw,88px) clamp(22px,7vw,100px);background:#1a3322;color:#faf7f2}.media-hero h1{color:#faf7f2;max-width:13ch;font:600 clamp(38px,5vw,64px)/1.04 "Cormorant Garamond",serif}.media-hero p{color:#e6dfd3;line-height:1.85;max-width:58ch}.media-hero img{display:block;width:100%;height:clamp(240px,34vw,430px);object-fit:cover;object-position:center 45%;border-radius:12px;box-shadow:0 18px 42px #0003}@media(max-width:720px){.media-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:42px 22px}.media-hero img{height:260px}}</style>
</SiteLayout>